   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## 1b. CPAZMaL data exploration (run only when DATASET_TYPE == \"cpazmal\")\n",
    "\n",
    "This section investigates hypotheses about why CPAZMaL classification performance is limited:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Geographic group imbalance** — with `max_train_samples` stratified by class only, a class's\n",
    "   training samples may all come from a single geographic group → non-representative barycenter.\n",
    "2. **NaN / invalid pixels** — SAR windows with nodata/negative values reduce effective N per timestep.\n",
    "3. **Parametric fit quality** — does Weibull (MLE vs log-cumulant) actually fit the SAR pixel\n",
    "   distribution? A high KS statistic indicates poor fit.\n",
    "4. **Barycenter stability** — with very few training samples (5–20), are barycenters stable?\n",
    "\n",
    "Cells below use the `data` dict from Cell 4 (which includes `groups` and `group_names`).\n",
    "Skip this section for synthetic data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "f1edca6e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
